Aim: Write an Embedded C Program to interface PIC18FXXX with LED and & blinking it
using specified delay.
Experimental SetUp : MPLAB X IDE v6.20, MicroPIC18F board, USB cable, Power Supply
adaptor, PICLoader software.
Procedure :
Step 1: Open MPLABX IDE on the PC for program development and create a new project and
save it in a new folder.
Step 2: Write the program in C language for interfacing LEDs to PIC18F4550. (in program
make sure to add the 0x800 offset)
Step 3: Build the program and create a hex file. In case of errors, correct the program and rebuild
to create a hex file.
Step 4: Prepare the experimental setup by connecting the MicroPIC18F board to the PC using
USB cable. Power ON the Board. Check for USBtoSerial COMx allocated by the PC.
Step 5: Using the PICLoader Software flash the hex file in the PIC18F4550.
Step 6: Press reset button and execute the program .
Result: Check if the LEDs are blinking. You can change the delay and vary the blinking rate.
Program:
